The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (!(ub->dev_info.flags & (UBLK_F_SUPPORT_ZERO_COPY |
                                    UBLK_F_AUTO_BUF_REG)))
        return false;
Reason: This condition only returns false (i.e., does not reset references) for devices using UBLK_F_SUPPORT_ZERO_COPY or UBLK_F_AUTO_BUF_REG, but omits UBLK_F_USER_COPY. After commit e63d2228ef83 optimized __ublk_fail_req() to skip decrementing the reference count, requests in USER_COPY mode retain a leaked reference (UBLK_REFCOUNT_INIT) when the server exits, allowing stale operations and triggering warnings.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!ublk_dev_need_req_ref(ub))
        return false;
Reason: The helper function ublk_dev_need_req_ref() returns true for all data copy modes that require reference counting (including UBLK_F_USER_COPY). This ensures that when the server exits, any outstanding requests in any reference-counted mode have their reference counts reset to 0, preventing the leak and its associated problems.

